\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Russian rouble jumps after bad inflation number  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski  \par \uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2006\par 08:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds Putin's aide comment in para 5-6)  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Russia's consumer price index rose by a worse-than-expected 0.2 percent in August, data showed on Tuesday, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the rouble to rise as it seeks to curb persistent price pressures.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble traded at 29.68 to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket -- made up of $0.6 and 0.4 euros -- up 0.4 percent from Monday's close. The rouble <RUBUTSTN=MCX> also reached its highest against the dollar since Dec. 1999.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts and traders said the rise in prices in August -- a month when they traditionally fall -- led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step back from the exchange rate level it had defended since mid-July.  \par \par \uc2 "Obviously, the bad inflation data pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into doing this. There were no other reasons for the rouble to go up," said Ruslan Tongiyev, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Petrokommerts Bank in Moscow.  \par \par \uc2 President Vladimir Putin's aide Igor Shuvalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's method of tying up money supply was not helping prices and acknowledged that annual inflation may overshoot the government's 9 percent target.  \par \par \uc2 "The rouble is firming so much, but inflation is not coming down -- everything testifies to the fact that with such strengthening (of the rouble) we will not meet the set parameters and inflation will be a little higher," Shuvalov told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 No comment was available from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Economy Minister German Gref stood by the government's annual inflation forecast for 2006 of 9.0 percent despite the August uptick.  \par \par \uc2 "We are sticking to our forecast, 0.2 percent is higher than we expected but it is not critical," Gref told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take out some of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $600 million a day in oil and gas export revenues but, concerned by the runaway growth in the money supply that results, has let the rouble rise in several small steps this year.  \par \par \uc2 In allowing the rouble to appreciate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is attracting speculative bets on further gains, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not think it is a good idea to let the rouble rise now. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using the tool it is familiar with, but this move is likely to provoke speculators into buying roubles," said Yevgeny Nadorshin, economist at Trust Bank.  \par \par \uc2 OPPOSITION TO STRONG ROUBLE  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last let the rouble rise on July 17, by 0.3 percent against the basket. The latest move follows record dollar purchases in August by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose $259 billion hoard of gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the world's third largest.  \par \par \uc2 However, opposition to further rouble strengthening among Russian exporters is rising, especially among metal and mining firms whose margins are squeezed by a strong national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , creating a policy dilemma the government has yet to solve.  \par \par \uc2 President Vladimir Putin told Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin last month to curb rouble appreciation because it hurts domestic industry.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble has now risen by 4.3 percent to the basket since the start of the year. It is up by 8 percent against the dollar and virtually unchanged against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Russia's money supply, which economists see as the key factor behind high inflation, rose by 45 percent in year-on-year terms as of Aug. 1. Excess liquidity drives up retail prices as well as prices for real estate and stocks.  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters had expected prices to rise by a median 0.1 percent in August, while the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had predicted a modest fall in prices.  \par \par \uc2 The food component of the CPI basket fell by 0.5 percent because abundant fruit and vegetables became cheaper while prices for non-food items and services climbed by 0.8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said petrol price hikes, a poor grain harvest and botched reforms to alcohol sales licences were behind the bad number. Prices rose by 7.1 percent in the year to date, closing in on the government's 2006 target.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult to see them hitting 9 percent by the end of the year, it would be good if they get under 10 percent," said Yevgeni Gavrilenkov, chief economist at Troika Dialog.  \par \par \uc2 Gref said the cabinet would continue consultations with oil firms on capping retail gasoline prices, which, he said, were the culprit behind the bad number in August.  \par \par \uc2 "There is nowhere for them (gasoline prices) to grow further, we will appeal to our previous agreements," Gref said, referring to a moratorium on rising gasoline prices reached with oil firms last year. (Additional reporting by Artyom Danielyan, James Kilner and Christian Lowe)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RUSSIA-ROUBLE (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060905e295000b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
