\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Rouble to rise but market guessing how much  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski  \par \uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 10:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 7 (Reuters) - The rouble is set to rise as Russian policy makers have made it clear they are ready to use the exchange rate to rein in inflation, but analysts remain divided over how much appreciation they will tolerate.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble <RUBUTSTN=MCX> has appreciated by 2.5 percent this year in nominal terms against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, comprised of dollars and euros, used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guide its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volumes have hit record levels, peaking on Feb. 8 amid market speculation that the authorities would allow the rouble to make a big move higher.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took out all dollar offers in that session, and expects to keep piling up foreign reserves -- up by 12 percent this year to $196 billion -- as it tries to stop the rouble from turning into an overvalued petro-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The big question is whether this is just another trading opportunity on the back of the dollar-euro trade, or whether this is the start of the long awaited next step-up in the rouble," said Chris Weafer, chief strategist at Alfa-Bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prints roubles to buy excess dollars flowing into Russia as a result of massive oil revenues. Its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  create a liquidity wave which is driving up prices for goods and assets like stocks and property.  \par \par \uc2 Prices in Russia grew by 10.9 percent in 2005. Big hikes in household utility charges and food prices mean that, just two months into the year, the consumer price index has risen by almost half the government's full-year target of 8.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 President Vladimir Putin berated ministers on Monday for letting prices get out of control and a row has broken out between the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over what remedial action to take.  \par \par \uc2 A senior Economy Ministry official told Reuters last week that the only way to curb prices would be to allow the rouble to rise in nominal terms. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded by hiking its deposit rates, although analysts said that would achieve little.  \par \par \uc2 "The trend is clearly towards more strengthening," said Zsolt Papp, emerging markets economist at ABN Amro, suggesting the rouble could test the level of 27 to the dollar towards the end of the year. It traded at around 28 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 NEUTRAL EXPECTATIONS  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters this month saw the rouble at 28.05 to the dollar by the end of March, 28.75 by mid-year and 27.75 by year's end.  \par \par \uc2 Central bankers say they have succeeded in creating neutral expectations on the exchange rate, as a result keeping market interest rates high enough to have a dampening effect on prices.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, which is 'reset' every morning and operates from 10 a.m. (0700 GMT) to 5 p.m. (1400 GMT), has succeeded in reducing market volatility, but has not removed the need for sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates that with oil prices at around $60 per barrel, it must buy $7 billion a month, but analysts say the bank's presence in the market may decrease as it tries to prepare markets for convertibility of the rouble.  \par \par \uc2 "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving towards full convertibility of the rouble and trying to prepare markets for that, I think it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less and less," said Papp.  \par \par \uc2 CONVERTIBILITY  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to lift capital controls, which include deposit requirements of up to 20 percent on capital account transactions, later this year.  \par \par \uc2 The move will pave the way for full rouble convertibility but at the same time may expose Russia to the risk of speculative capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "It is a positive signal and should support the rouble going forward. The fact that money will be able to circulate more freely should also boost investment," said Elisabeth Gruie, emerging markets strategist at BNP Paribas in London.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts also said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeds in reining in inflation it might be instructed to reverse the rising trend around mid-year to protect domestic producers.  \par \par \uc2 "I would not be surprised if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is instructed by policy makers to reverse the current trend of rouble appreciation," Papp said. (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao in London)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-RUSSIA-ROUBLE (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060310e237000nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
