\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Slower growth, faster inflation to trouble Russia  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Meg Clothier and Artyom Danielyan  \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2005\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 1 (Reuters) - Russia's goals for economic growth and inflation this year and next remain excessively optimistic, a Reuters poll of 15 economists showed on Thursday, while its fiscal position is top-notch.  \par \par \uc2 The future of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is harder to call. Analysts' forecasts diverge sharply, with most seeing the rouble rising against the dollar while a significant minority expect it to weaken. The survey predicts Russia will have managed to nail consumer price growth flat in August, a glimmer of improvement for a data series that has disappointed for most of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Economists forecast gross domestic product growth slipping to a median 5.7 percent this year and 5.3 percent next year after two years of expansion above 7 percent. The 2005 forecast is markedly weaker than last month's 6.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Full-year inflation is seen at 12 percent in 2005 and 10 percent in 2006, well above government targets. For a full table of poll results, please click on [ID:nL30724029].  \par \par \uc2 Analysts did, however, say there was a marked improvement in the business climate, after the pursuit of oil firm YUKOS and other companies for back tax bills proved such a menace to investors' faith in Russia.  \par \par \uc2 "It's impossible to say economic policy has acquired a liberal bias," said Anton Stroutchenevski at Troika Dialog. "But it has to be acknowledged that there are fewer of the aggressive attacks that have been disturbing the business community."  \par \par \uc2 SHOULDER THE BURDEN  \par \par \uc2 Although retail sales growth has been strong this year, underpinned by Russians' rising salaries, the industrial sector is flagging -- full year growth is expected to be 4.8 percent this year after 7.3 percent last year.  \par \par \uc2 And Russia's key natural resources sector is growing at a fraction of the pace of manufacturing.  \par \par \uc2 "Real appreciation of the rouble and a high tax burden on the oil sector remain some of the main obstacles to growth in industrial production," Raiffeisenbank noted.  \par \par \uc2 Only three economists thought Russia could drag 2005 inflation below last year's 11.7 percent -- the government is still officially hoping for 11 percent. Nor did anybody set any store by a target of 8.5 percent that is in place for next year.  \par \par \uc2 "Summer deflation, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hoping for, will barely be achieved this year, largely because of a new upturn in petrol prices and the continuing effect of earlier tariff price rises," said Uralsib's Vladimir Tikhomirov.  \par \par \uc2 As for the rouble, which at the moment takes its cue from swings in the euro/dollar rate globally, the poll shows it at a median 28.20 to the dollar at the close of 2005, firming to 27.25 at the end of 2006.  \par \par \uc2 However, by then the predictions range from 25 to 29.1 to the dollar, evidence of split views firstly about the direction Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is likely to take and secondly about investor sentiment towards the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  longer term.  \par \par \uc2 Massive oil receipts and hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases during market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should nudge \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves well past the $200 billion mark by the end of next year and up to $175 billion this year.  \par \par \uc2 And, despite a move to ease fiscal policy and spend a chunk of oil money in the run-up to presidential elections in 2008, analysts expect healthy budget surpluses this year and next.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Maria Kiselyova)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-RUSSIA-POLL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050901e191000zv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
