\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian c.bank begins rouble/euro  \highlight22\uc2 operations \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Artyom Danielyan and Douglas Busvine   \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2005\par 15:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with background, analysts)   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had begun \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the rouble/euro market as it continues a drive to wean the market off its fixation with the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The move, signalled well in advance, comes as the Bank of Russia seeks to broaden the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to better reflect burgeoning trade flows with Europe and prepare for the removal of capital controls by 2007.   \par \par \uc2 But it does not herald an immediate increase in the share of euros in Russia's big \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which at nearly $150 billion are the largest of any country outside Asia, a top central banker said.   \par \par \uc2 There is "absolutely no connection", \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Chairman Konstantin Korishchenko told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 Korishchenko added that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to buy euros, it could now do so by selling roubles, whereas previously it had to buy and then sell dollars as an intermediary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  runs a 'dirty' rouble float, typically buying dollars to stem upward pressures on the rouble arising from high prices for oil, Russia's main export, and defend the competitiveness of domestic industry.   \par \par \uc2 The rouble has fallen by around 2 percent against the resurgent dollar year-to-date, but is up by 8 percent against the euro.   \par \par \uc2 VOLUMES UP   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia said in a statement it had begun rouble/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug. 25, in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket comprising 0.35 euros and $0.65 it uses to guide its day-to-day exchange rate policy.   \par \par \uc2 Trade in euros for 'tomorrow' delivery jumped to 23 million euros on Thursday and 18 million euros on Friday, well above typical volumes, figures from the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICEX) showed.   \par \par \uc2 But, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added, the dollar would remain the core of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, "where the situation determines the official exchange rate of the rouble and the scale of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy remains heavily dollarised, with the greenback a safe haven for many Russians who suffered painful losses in the hyperinflation and financial crashes of the 1990s.   \par \par \uc2 Euros account for 30-35 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and despite Korishchenko's assurances to the contrary, analysts expect that share to rise gradually over time.   \par \par \uc2 "This is the experience of the countries that do have in place these \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket regimes," said Yaroslav Lissovolik, an economist at United Financial Group in Moscow.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts agree that broadening the market reduces pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defence of a target exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 They also say that a well diversified market should make it easier for policymakers to fight inflation running at around 13 percent -- above the government's year-end target of 11 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "It has taken very long to get here but it's very welcome," said Lars Christensen, economist at Danske Bank in Copenhagen. "Now we need to see an appreciation of the rouble, which is a politically hard process to handle ... to reduce inflation."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 operational currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket early this year and has increased the share of euros in small steps. Analysts expect the euro to end up with a weighting of at least half of the basket.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket should not be confused with the trade-weighted basket used to calculate the real effective exchange rate, a measure used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside inflation to guide its policy.   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-RUSSIA-CBANK (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050826e18q0019q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
