\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  could start rouble/euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  -cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vlasta Demyanenko  \par \uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2005\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds analysts' comments, edits)  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it may begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the rouble/euro market later this year as the euro becomes increasingly important to the country's economy and trade.  \par \par \uc2 Rouble/euro trade <EURRUBON=MCX> accounts for as little as 1 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes on Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICEX) with dollar/rouble dominant.  \par \par \uc2 But the Bank of Russia is raising the euro's profile -- over half of Russia's foreign trade is with Europe -- increasing the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's share in the basket it uses to manage the rouble rate day-to-day.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the rouble/dollar market -- as dealers said it did on Thursday -- to smooth out exchange rate fluctuations. But it plans to scale back its presence in the run-up to lifting capital controls in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 "In some ways this will be a substitute for rouble/dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Deputy Chairman Konstantin Korishchenko told a panel discussion. He said a decision was in the offing but there was no precise timeframe as yet.  \par \par \uc2 SECOND FIDDLE  \par \par \uc2 There are plans to support euro liquidity, with a new rouble/euro contract for "tomorrow" settlement planned for early June, as well as a longer trading session of at least 3-1/2 hours, said MICEX General Director Alexander Potyomkin.  \par \par \uc2 However, as long as Russia's commodity exports continue to be priced in dollars, the euro will play second fiddle.  \par \par \uc2 "Not only are most of the current account flows dollarised, but also the man on the street thinks in dollars which is why I don't think we'll see euro unseat the economic importance of the dollar," said Jens Nystedt, a Deutsche Bank economist in London.  \par \par \uc2 "I still see the rouble/euro as a derivative of the main rouble/U.S. dollar cross but they are heading in the right direction," he added, saying the share of euro trade might hit 20 percent in five or six years.  \par \par \uc2 DUAL BASKET  \par \par \uc2 Russia uses a dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket to guide the rouble's nominal exchange rate intraday. This is different from the basket with which it measures its real effective exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 At the moment the proportions are 0.2 euros and $0.8, but Korishchenko reiterated that the bank will change this to 0.3 euros soon. Analysts expect the amount of euros and dollars to become roughly even over time.  \par \par \uc2 The key result of the dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket has been for the rouble/dollar to shoulder more of the volatility stemming from moves on global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 "Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to maintain the rouble/dollar rate unchanged for a week or two at a time. Then if there was clearly a new trend in the euro/dollar it would change its (dollar) bid by 10 kopecks," said Troika Dialog chief economist Yevgeny Gavrilenkov.  \par \par \uc2 "Now it does this on an everyday basis. It has become more adaptable to global fluctuations."  \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not dip in and out of the market, Russia's booming oil export receipts would drive the rouble higher, killing domestic producers' competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the funnelling of windfall oil revenues into a budget stabilisation fund, the rouble is still appreciating fast -- by 6.6 percent in real, trade-weighted terms in the first four months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 "We would like to try to reduce the level of our involvement in the market, which is hard at the moment, but that is the direction we are trying to move in," Korishchenko added.  \par \par \uc2 Potyomkin also said the share of euros in Russia's gold and foreign reserves was around 25-30 percent, in line with recent comments by officials.  \par \par \uc2 Any suggestion Russia is preparing to raise the euro share can boost the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on global markets. Russia's reserves, the largest outside Asia, have hit a new record high of $144.7 billion, weekly data showed on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RUSSIA-EURO (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050512e15c0015y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
