\par\par \b \uc2 Russia rouble hits month-highs, cbank cuts dlr bid.   \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2005\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Feb 18 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble hit month-highs against the dollar on Friday, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in and support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 27.93 roubles, dealers said.    \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was riding high on its two favourite bull signals - gloomy inflation data at home and a lacklustre dollar abroad.    \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to say exactly why the bank lowered its dollar bid - but its either high inflation or a firm euro (against the dollar)," one dealer said.    \par \par \uc2  By 1110 GMT roubles for "tomorrow" delivery  were up 0.2 percent at 27.9405, having been fixed at 27.9998 the previous session. They peaked at 27.9200.    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought dollars at 28.00 roubles the previous session, dealers said.    \par \par \uc2  On global markets the dollar hovered near a recent two-week low against the euro, with investors torn between strong U.S. economic data and worries about long-term damage to the dollar from the U.S. current account deficit.    \par \par \uc2  Late on Thursday Russian presidential advisor Andrei Illarionov told Reuters consumer price growth in the first two weeks of February was 0.7 percent, after 2.6 percent in the whole of January.    \par \par \uc2  This could mean 4 percent price growth in the first two months of the year was not out of the question, making the government's target of 8.5 percent for 2005 look "interesting", he said.    \par \par \uc2  In Russia, a country where a tighter monetary policy means a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say the best way to combat stubborn inflation would be a stronger rouble.    \par \par \uc2  "Anticipation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the rouble appreciate faster as a response to fast CPI is growing," Vneshtorgbank head of treasury research, Nikolai Kascheev, said in a note.    \par \par \uc2  Standard & Poor's, the last of the Big Three ratings agencies to award Russia investment grade status, has also added its voice to calls to for rouble appreciation, saying it would combat \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case of "Dutch disease".    \par \par \uc2  Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was unsustainable, it said, and a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would force domestic industry to reform by undermining the competitive advantage an undervalued rouble had given them.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050218e12i00aq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
