\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-IMF urges Russian reforms to restore growth.   \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2005\par 00:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund on Wednesday said investors' doubts about Russia's commitment to market-orientated reforms and a perception of increased state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slowed investment growth.   \par \par \uc2 In a statement issued at the end of annual economic talks in Moscow, the IMF said the drop in investment growth and lower oil export volumes had slowed Russian growth since mid-2004, despite high oil prices.   \par \par \uc2 "In the mission's view, boldly launching long-delayed structural reforms - not least administrative and civil service reforms - and ensuring the tax administration and other state agencies act in a transparent and even-handed manner are crucial for reassuring investors and restoring growth momentum," the IMF said.   \par \par \uc2 It also urged Russia not to spend more of its oil revenue windfall, which had added to inflation.   \par \par \uc2 The IMF said planned increases in pension benefits and other expenditures of more than 0.75 percent of GDP will add to budget pressures.   \par \par \uc2 Therefore it was becoming "a matter of urgency" to resist spending more oil revenue profits, while no further amendments to the 2005 budget should be considered, the fund added.   \par \par \uc2 "In line with this, the floor on the amount of resources in the (oil) stabilization fund that cannot be spent should be lifted to facilitate saving in full the oil windfall, except for that part that is allocated to the prepayment of external debt," the IMF said.   \par \par \uc2 Russia should also increase exchange rate flexibility, the fund said.   \par \par \uc2 It said unless \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and allow faster ruble appreciation if inflation deviates from the target, inflation was unlikely to fall in 2005.   \par \par \uc2 "The trade-off between reducing inflation and resisting ruble appreciation is likely to sharpen this year as the balance of payments is set to improve further, provided there is no repeat of the negative jolts to confidence that caused a sharp rise in capital flows in 2004," it said.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050216e12g00l5c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
