\par\par \b \uc2 Russia's gold/ \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves hit new record high.  \b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $4.5 billion in the week to Dec 3. to hit a new record high of $121.6 billion, data showed on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2  High prices for \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief export oil and dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen rouble appreciation have driven reserves growth.   \par \par \uc2  Russia's reserves, up by half since the start of this year, are the largest outside Asia. They now outstrip Russia's public foreign debt and already exceed Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin's latest year-end forecast of $120 billion.   \par \par \uc2  Russia's fast-growing reserves have made \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets sensitive to any hint it might increase the proportion of euros it holds - at the expense of the weak dollar.   \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was "thinking about" changing its reserves mix but said no decision had been taken yet.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c9005sh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
