\par\par \b \uc2 Russia rouble at 4-year high vs dlr, cbank steps in.   \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 6 (Reuters) - The rouble rose to new four-year highs against a globally weak dollar on Monday, prompting the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars and check the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb.   \par \par \uc2 The rouble's peak came at 27.8250 to the dollar, its strongest since November 2000, before it slipped back by 1020 GMT to trade at 27.8650 - still firmer than its fixing at 27.9271 the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBR), which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically to stem rouble appreciation, buying dollars at around 27.8250 to 27.8300.   \par \par \uc2 With the greenback under pressure and Russia needing to combat inflation, analysts say the rouble's rise looks set to continue. It has already gained nearly 5 percent against the dollar in less than two months.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows continued focus on the euro/dollar exchange rate," said Metallinvestbank dealer Sergei Romanchuk.   \par \par \uc2 The greenback fetched $1.3449 against the euro , having fallen to around $1.3460 on Friday in the wake of a disappointing U.S. payrolls report.   \par \par \uc2 "The downslide of the dollar goes on forever. Sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the CBR are probably the only ... unpredictable market factor," Vneshtorgbank said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers say it is always difficult to predict the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves - and the bank itself says it never comments on the specifics of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2 For much of this year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the rouble artificially depressed to spur competitiveness, which economists warned would fuel inflation. The authorities say prices could rise as much as 11.5 percent this year, above an original 10 percent target.   \par \par \uc2 Consumer price data for November is due to be released at 1200 GMT. Analysts polled by Reuters predict price growth of 1.1 percent month-on-month, the same as the previous month and the fastest since January.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041206e0c60074d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
