\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  rouble gropes for cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level.   \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 13:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble retreated from Thursday's 7-month highs against the dollar on Friday, trading cautiously as dealers said they had tried and failed to discover where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would next cap Russia's buoyant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A falling dollar on global markets has added to rouble appreciation pressure stemming from high prices for Russia's major export, oil, driving the rouble within sight of multi-year highs.   \par \par \uc2 "We tried to grope for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (dollar) bid, but it is not there yet," said Viktor Anisimov, an Aljba Alliance dealer.   \par \par \uc2 By 1230 GMT the rouble for "tomorrow" settlement was little changed in official trade at 28.5375 to the dollar, having been fixed at 28.5387 the previous session. On Thursday, it hit 28.5101, the highest since early April, which was when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to a weaker rouble policy to help exporters.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that if the dollar wilted further against the euro next week, the rouble could challenge year-highs around 28.45. "A battle will start at 28.45, that's a level we won't go through quickly," Anisimov added.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Chairman Konstantin Korishchenko told Reuters that Russia could not keep the rouble stable if the dollar was falling on global markets, which dealers saw as bullish for the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets real rouble apprecation against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , giving the bank leeway to allow the rouble to rise against the dollar if the greenback weakens against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 But analysts say appreciation against the dollar is proving unpopular. "We ... understand that there has been significant political lobbying on the part of the domestic manufacturing and mining sectors to keep the rouble nominally weak," Alexei Moisseev, a Renaissance Capital analyst, said in a note.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041119e0bj009nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
