\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble slips, cbanker comments weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2004\par 14:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble softened against the dollar on Wednesday, retreating after a top central banker said the rouble would end the year flat-to-weaker if the euro/dollar rate stayed the same, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Current trends in the nominal (rouble/dollar) rate strongly depend on the euro/dollar rate, and if that relationship remains unchanged then the exchange rate at the end of the year will be between 28.6 and 29 roubles to the dollar," First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said.  \par \par \uc2 Effective rouble appreciation against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be 6 percent or a little more this year, he added, well inside a government target of no more than 7 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Ulyukayev of course gave hope to dollar bulls," said one dealer. "But he did not say where the exchange rate would be if the euro is at $1.20 or $1.35."  \par \par \uc2 By 1300 GMT roubles for 'tomorrow' delivery slipped to 28.6775 to the dollar in official trade, having been fixed at 28.6502 the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was down on the day at around $1.2970 per euro, struggling above record lows hit earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 However, dealers thought the rouble would perk up quickly.  \par \par \uc2 "The market will steady at current levels with export revenues arriving. Then it will seek out the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ('s dollar support level)," said Zenit bank dealer Alexander Karpov.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically to stop oil-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange inflows driving the rouble sharply higher, which would undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 It last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a dollar bid of 28.6450 roubles on Tuesday, but with the rouble weakening it was absent from the market this session, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed the rouble to rise nearly 2 percent against the dollar in the last month in what it calls an adjustment to account for broad dollar weakness, but analysts say it is trying to dampen inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev said he saw inflation at 10.5 percent to 11 percent this year, above a now largely discredited government target of 10 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041110e0ba00a6q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
