\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Central European  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  await US vote.  \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2004\par 15:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 2 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held their breath on Tuesday with few domestic factors available to offset the uncertainty gripping global markets over U.S. presidential elections.  \par \par \uc2 A repeat of the drawn-out courtroom wranglings for the White House between Republicans and Democrats of four years ago would leave the United States without a decisive leader and could weaken the dollar and unsettle global markets, analysts and traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "It was pretty unseemly then and for it to happen twice in four years to the world super-power would be the worst result possible (for the dollar)," a London-based rand trader said.  \par \par \uc2 If the dollar lost ground against the euro it would also knock back many of the central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which are traded mainly against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At 1340 GMT the Polish zloty traded slightly stronger against the euro at week highs of 4.3011 , while the Hungarian forint was steady at 245.55 per euro .  \par \par \uc2 Graham Stock, emerging markets strategist at JP Morgan, said the best result for central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a clear victory. He also said they were not as vulnerable as southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that an indecisive U.S. election result would cause.  \par \par \uc2 "Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are slightly more immune because their performance is linked in with euro convergence and ERM-2. They are becoming more and more divorced from the emerging markets world," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Many European Union newcomers want to join the euro by the end of this decade and some have already entered the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ante-chamber, the ERM-2.  \par \par \uc2 FREE THE ROUBLE  \par \par \uc2 Russia's finance minister Alexei Kudrin told Reuters in an interview that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should free up the rouble to curb inflationary pressures.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars, but in recent weeks has allowed the rouble to appreciate by around 1.5 percent against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 However, Kudrin's comments had little impact in the closely-controlled rouble which softened slightly against the dollar to 28.7845 , compared to Monday's 28.7651 close. It remained close to a recent six-month high.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to increase in the future.  \par \par \uc2 "In the past few weeks we have seen increasing number of comments from Russian officials talking about increasing the rouble's value against the dollar," Wike Groenenberg, emerging markets strategist at Citibank, said.  \par \par \uc2 "The actual rouble decisions are made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Kudrin is definitely somebody they would talk to and listen to," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041102e0b2008t9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
