\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  c.bank aims for less  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2004\par 16:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes new monetary instruments could allow it to scale down its frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a top bank official said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently steps in to buy back dollars and cap the rouble, which it wants to keep at competitive levels. But pumping roubles into the economy causes inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 "We are determined that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be the exception rather than the rule in situations where there is a danger of some volatility," First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev told a parliamentary budget committee.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on government securities are below inflation, meaning Russian banks prefer to park excess money in dollars, prompting a flood of dollar-selling when banks need roubles to pay taxes at the end of each month.  \par \par \uc2 "We want banks to raise money more through our refinancing instruments," Ulyukayev added.  \par \par \uc2 A refusal by big banks to lend to small banks on the interbank market was one of the reasons behind a mini-banking crisis this summer.  \par \par \uc2 The bank wants to add corporate and regional debt to the range of instruments banks can use as collateral for short-term refinancing deals with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Banks can already exchange government debt when they need cash.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also revived its own OBR bonds after nearly three years, with an issue slated for Oct. 6. Earlier this week Ulyukayev said he expected the issue to yield a little over 6 percent to a July 15, 2005 put option.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees inflation in 2005 of 6.5 to 8.5 percent, down from this year's 10 percent target.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040930e09u00cku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
