\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia to hit  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 , inflation targets-c.bank.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Artyom Danielyan  \par \uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2004\par 14:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was on course to meet its twin policy targets for inflation and the rouble this year, despite market expectations that price growth will overshoot its 10 percent goal.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also signalled it may cut its refinancing rate to 12 percent from 13 percent this year, although this would be a largely symbolic move because its management of the exchange rate blunts interest rates as a policy tool.  \par \par \uc2 First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev forecast the rouble would end 2004 barely changed in nominal terms at between 29.22 and 29.50 roubles to the U.S. dollar . Monday's day-ahead rouble fix was 29.2164.  \par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev said the real effective exchange rate - which strips out differences in inflation - would rise by just below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 7 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 He also forecast that monthly inflation would be zero in September, down from a rise of 0.4 percent in August which led some analysts to say the full-year target of 10 percent was no longer realistic.  \par \par \uc2 "We count on fulfilling these two fundamental tasks," Ulyukayev told a Brunswick UBS investment conference.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities run a dual policy regime, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar buying to neutralise appreciation pressure stemming from record oil export earnings.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to bring down inflation gradually - although that goal has come under threat from the rouble liquidity generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 The authorities have taken some action to keep liquidity from flooding into the economy - including channelling oil windfall gains into a government stabilisation fund and issuing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds to soak up roubles.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and recent Eurobond issues by Russian corporates are boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which Ulyukayev forecast would reach "a little more than" $100 billion by the end of this year.  \par \par \uc2 Reserves rose to a new all-time high of $92.6 billion on Sept. 17 from $90.0 billion on Sept. 10, the bank said last week. They were $77 billion at the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Commenting on interest rates, Ulyukayev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut its 13 percent refinancing rate by up to one point by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "It is possible, although we promise nothing, that we will lower it before the end of the year. I think it will not be less than 12 percent," Ulyukayev said.  \par \par \uc2 Commercial banks do not usually borrow from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this rate but it is commonly used as a reference rate for overdue payments by banks and companies.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term interbank rates are now 3-5 percent - negative in real terms.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last lowered the refinancing rate during a mini-banking crisis in June of this year, by one percent from 14 percent, in a bid to shore up confidence.   \par \par 