\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Euro gains firmer footing in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves contest.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2004\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 28 (Reuters) - The euro is gaining ground as a credible rival to the dollar and moves by emerging market central banks to diversify their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are likely to give the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  long-term support.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks around the world have slowly been buying euros since its birth in 1999 to diversify dollar-dominated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, minimise risks and enhance returns.  \par \par \uc2 Now Russia, which keeps a tight grip on the rouble, is planning to replace dollar-based monitoring of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a dollar/euro basket, which could entail buying euros to curb rouble strength.  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said last week the country is diversifying its vast reserves out of dollars to include more European and Asian bonds. Libya also said it planned to change the peg for its dinar to give the euro a bigger weighting.  \par \par \uc2 "Diversification has been going on and it has played a big part in the euro's rally, when a growth gap between the United States and the euro zone is so wide. Given the size of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, even a 10 percent rise in a euro weighting means massive euro buying," said Jim McCormick, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Lehman Brothers.  \par \par \uc2 "Reserve management comes down to liquidity and trade flows. For return and confidence reasons the euro's share can go up to a 50-50 status with the dollar over the very long term."  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit a record high of $1.2927 in February. Since then, it has fallen 10 cents as financial market focus shifted to strength in the U.S. economy and expectations of higher interest rates. It stood at $1.19 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the International Monetary Fund showed the euro's share in official \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to 18.7 percent in 2002 from 12.7 in 1999. Demand for the dollar stood at 64.5 percent in 2002 compared with 67.9. 2003 data is due later this year.  \par \par \uc2 Global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves exceeded $3.2 trillion at the end of March, according to BNP Paribas using IMF data.  \par \par \uc2 "Part of the substantial euro buying last year was related to the rebalancing of reserves by central banks. It is clearly euro positive in the long term," said Mary Davis, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston.  \par \par \uc2 GRADUAL PROCESS  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to prevent the rouble from strengthening due to a rising current account surplus and capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Russia's current account surplus stood at $35.9 billion at the end of 2003, up from $29.1 in 2002. Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves rose to $83.2 billion in April from $57.7 billion a year ago, reflecting increased dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 CSFB estimates \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will reach $90 billion by the end of 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said under the new basket scheme, the euro would represent 10 to 20 percent of the basket and its weight would gradually rise to 50 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say such a basket composition is more consistent with Russia's trade relationships. Mostly commodity-based exports are priced in dollars and imports are mainly invoiced in euros.  \par \par \uc2 Using a trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  link and Russia's current account surplus, BNP Paribas estimates the introduction of the basket will create additional euro demand of around 10-15 billion euros each year, supporting the euro in the long term.  \par \par \uc2 In China, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator Guo Shuqing said in a newspaper interview last week the country wants to move towards a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system that would link the yuan to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than just to the dollar as at present.  \par \par \uc2 China holds the majority of its $440 billion reserves, the world's second largest, in dollars.  \par \par \uc2 In India, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already been diversifying its reserves out of dollars into the euro. The Indian rupee is linked to a basket of four \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the dollar, euro, sterling and yen - and the government is considering reforms of its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime towards eventual full flotation.  \par \par \uc2 "Diversification means central banks would sell U.S. assets to buy other assets and, as an adequate reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro is in a prominent position," said Hans Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040428e04s002iv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
