\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  cbank ups  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  rate to curb rouble.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Julie Tolkacheva  \par \uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2004\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, April 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its rouble \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate on Monday for the first time in three months after its chairman promised President Vladimir Putin he would curb the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is hurting local producers.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble, which has gained almost five percent against the euro-dollar basket since the start of the year, fell almost five kopecks against the dollar and dealers said they expected a further nominal weakening.  \par \par \uc2 Its strength has been caused by a heavy inflow of dollars from the country's oil exports, the backbone of Russia's economy, heavy corporate borrowing abroad and Russians switching their savings from dollars into roubles.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble fell in early official trade on Monday to a weighted average for tomorrow settlement of 28.5535 per dollar compared with 28.5065 the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to buy $200 million at 28.5250 a dollar, or four kopecks more than before.  \par \par \uc2 "As soon as banks saw the bid, everything became clear," said Alfa bank dealer Alexei Bukleyev.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had changed its bid after Friday's meeting between \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev and Putin. Ignatyev promised to curb the rouble's gains against the dollar to seven percent this year, a level which he said would not hurt local companies.  \par \par \uc2 A firmer rouble erodes the competitiveness of local goods and may threaten Putin's target of doubling the size of the economy within a decade.  \par \par \uc2 Nikolai Kashcheyev, an analyst at Trust investment bank, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have changed its priorities to containing the rouble's strength from controlling inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The rouble has firmed 4.7 percent against a basket of the dollar and euro since the start of 2004 compared with a 4.1 percent gain in the whole of 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Consumer price inflation stood at 3.5 percent in the first quarter. Russia targets a 10 percent annual inflation rate and with prices usually weaker in summer months the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in a position to achieve the goal easily.  \par \par \uc2 ROUBLE SEEN DOWN  \par \par \uc2 Bukleyev said that given current inflation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to make sure the rouble was traded at around 29 per dollar by the end of the year if it wants to prevent it from firming by more than seven percent.  \par \par \uc2 "That is why I think that(C) Reuters Limited 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040412e04c002nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
