\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble slips vs dollar,cbank reserves fall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 4 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble fell marginally against the dollar on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its support floor for the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after selling over $1 billion from its reserves the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for today settlement eased to 28.6653 per dollar from a weighted average of 28.5888 per dollar the previous session, when it shed about 10 kopecks in response to sharp gains by the greenback on global markets.  \par \par \uc2 Roubles for delivery on Friday fell to 28.72 per dollar in early hours of trade but rebounded to 28.6250 by 1050 GMT after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $80-100 million to offset downward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's offer served as a signal it would not tolerate excessive volatility in the market. (The move) worked, and the rouble rebounded as banks apparently opted to re-open short positions," Sergei Romanchuk at Metallinvestbank said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which looked unwilling to run down its reserves ahead of $2.5 billion in foreign debt payments due in March, moved its offer to sell dollars to 28.6950 from 28.6350 on Wednesday, when it sold more than $1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 UFG investment house said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were nothing to worry about as \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solid balance of payments remained intact and no signs of major capital outflows were seen.  \par \par \uc2 The investment house suggested the rouble was likely to resume its upwards path after March 14 presidential elections thanks to high global crude prices and traditionally higher capital inflows in the second quarter of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "Market liquidity should hence remain strong until at least July, when seasonal worsening of the balance of payments usually kicks in," UFG said in its market comment.  \par \par \uc2 Also on Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been buying dollars from the market for most of last month to contain the rise of the rouble, reported its gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves shrank by $300 million to $86.4 billion on February 27.  \par \par \uc2 "It confirms market talk last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a minimum, as market participants have begun to cover dollar shorts given month-long \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support and euro/dollar weakness," Stanislav Gelfer, an analyst at 4Cast said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040304e03400182\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
