\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Russia cbank cuts refinancing rate by 300 bps. \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2003\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday announced a three percentage point cut in its refinancing rate in a move seen by analysts as guiding the market towards rouble rates more in line with those on hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instruments. \par \par \uc2  The bank said the rate would fall to 18 percent from 21 percent from February 17. \par \par \uc2  It made no comment on the move, which is in line with its strategy of regulating money supply through rates rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks do not usually borrow from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  using the refinancing rate, but it is frequently used as a reference rate for overdue payments by banks and companies. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, a popular instrument among banks to manage their rouble liquidity, are linked to an 18 percent overnight credit rate, which usually moves in line with the refinancing rate. \par \par \uc2  "The cut in the rate which currently plays a decorative role is of a psychological importance which is to guide the market towards lower rouble rates and bring them more in line with hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates," Denis Rodionov, a director at Brunswick UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  Last week a senior central banker told Reuters he saw room for lowering the refinancing rate because of falling yields on the local debt market and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to make it a policy tool. \par \par \uc2  The yields on rouble-denominated instruments started to slide after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped curbing the rouble's strength making investments to hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive and pushing banks to invest to treasuries or to extend more loans to the economy. \par \par \uc2  "This is an administrative rate cut that sets no benchmark to the market but it confirms their policy to reduce the rates on rouble denominated instruments," Sergei Shchepilov, a dealer at Reiffeisen Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The refinancing rate, which in most economies is a key tool in regulating liquidity, stopped being effective in Russia after the 1998 economic crisis which deprived commercial banks of the government securities market. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the market in government paper has been growing but is still seen too low to soak up much funds. \par \par \uc2  The new administration of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which took over last March, pledged that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would become the focal point for setting rates and regulating money supply. \par \par \uc2  Until recently, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulated money supply through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than rates. \par \par \uc2  The refinancing rate was last changed in August 2002, when it was cut from 23 percent. Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the refinancing rate three times. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030214dz2e00vyc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
