\par\par \b \uc2  Russian rouble falls as liquidity fears ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2003\par 13:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Jan 30 (Reuters) - A rouble rally against the dollar lost some of its steam on Thursday when money supply data eased concern about an end of month liquidity squeeze, pushing the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its lowest level in six trading days. \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 2.24 kopecks in official early trade  to a weighted average for settlement today of 31.8224 to the dollar from 31.8000 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The rouble has firmed in recent weeks, fuelled by high global crude prices that have boosted oil-rich \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export revenues. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occasions to cap the rouble's rise. \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the world's second-biggest oil exporter. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength were concerns that the rouble supply would dry up at the end of this month when local firms must make tax payments and banks have to meet reserve requirements. \par \par \uc2  "(But) overnight lending rates eased ...indicating that the rouble supply is not that bad for the end of the month," said Sergei Shchepilov, a dealer at Raiffeisen Bank. \par \par \uc2  By 1140 GMT rouble overnight rates hovered at 3.75/5.75 percent as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's data showed that banks' balances on their correspondent accounts  leapt to 91.9 billion roubles from 76.1 billion roubles on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Shchepilov said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases have helped to steady the market, hit earlier this month when two Russian oil firms drained almost 60 billion roubles to pay for a stake in a rival producer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been keeping a tight grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over past four trading days by buying dollars to contain the rouble at 31.80, did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Igor Bogdanchik, a dealer at Dialog Optim bank said that the rouble could ease another kopeck or so on Friday to about 31.83-31.84. "Market liquidity is now enough to believe that the rouble will not appreciate," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, roubles for Friday delivery  were quoted at 31.8250/31.8350 at 1125 GMT compared to 31.8175/31.8225 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030130dz1u00pgu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
