\par\par \b \uc2  Russia cenbank steps in again to halt rouble rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2003\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Jan 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth straight trading days on Wednesday to halt a rouble rally against the dollar that has been fuelled by oil export earnings. \par \par \uc2  The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely moved in official early trade  and stood at a weighted average for settlement today of 31.8000 to the dollar compared to 31.8001 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers traced the rouble's steadiness to the efforts of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which bought at least $200 million on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "A strong supply of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues from exports is balanced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying," said Valery Petrov, head of research at Rosbank. \par \par \uc2  "This \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stability is making it difficult for other market participants to bet on a higher or lower dollar rate." \par \par \uc2  The rouble has been propelled by oil-rich Russia's hefty foreign trade surplus. Oil prices have soared on fears that a war in Iraq could lead to supply disruptions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tries to contain the rouble's strength, often blamed for blunting the competitive edge of local producers, by buying dollars and putting them in its reserves. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the rouble to remain steady to moderately lower against the dollar over the next few sessions if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to resist its rise. \par \par \uc2  "Export revenues keep on flooding the market and the dollar would dive (against the rouble) the very moment the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  withdrew," said Artem Roshchin at Aljba Alliance bank. \par \par \uc2  They said there seemed to be little room for an abrupt drop in the value of the rouble given high crude prices and the dollar's weakness against the euro amid fears of a war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, another forum for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, roubles for Thursday delivery  were quoted at 31.8130-31.8230 at 1125 GMT, almost two kopecks lower compared to 31.7950/31.8010 seen at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030129dz1t00o2v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
