\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  rouble stable on fears of cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2002\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 22 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble was stable against the dollar on Thursday as banks were wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rouble firmed in official early trade, which serves as the basis for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next day rate, to a weighted average for today settlement of 31.5711 to the dollar from 31.5735 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, roubles for tomorrow delivery , stood at 31.5820/31.5920 a dollar, little changed from Wednesday's close of 31.5850/31.5900. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that it did not want to allow the dollar to go above 31.60," said Alfa-Bank dealer Alexei Bukleyev. \par \par \uc2  "That is why, seeing this and expecting a rouble shortage at the end of the month, banks started selling dollars on their own and creating short positions." \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  asked banks for quotes as soon as the rouble fell to 31.60 per dollar. Dealers said there was no evidence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in the market on either Wednesday or Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bukleyev expected the rouble to fluctuate in a range of 31.57/31.59 range for the remainder of the session. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020822dy8m00j5x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
