\par\par \b \uc2  Russian Ctrl Bank Reserves $36.2B Dec 14 Vs $36.1B Dec 7 \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2001\par 10:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW -(Dow Jones)- The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that its level of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves rose $100 million in the week to Dec. 14, to $36.2 billion. \par \par \uc2  A week earlier, Dec. 7, the reserves totaled $36.1 billion. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rarely comments on changes in its level of reserves, but market participants said the rise in reserves shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped supporting the ruble. A week earlier, the reserves dropped steeply as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the ruble. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves more than doubled in 2000, to $27.95 billion as of Jan. 1 this year, from $12.46 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following table illustrates the change in reserves over recent\par weeks:\par            Dec.  14       $36.2 Bln\par            Dec.   7       $36.1 Bln\par            Nov.  30       $37.3 Bln\par            Nov.  23       $38.6 Bln\par            Nov.  16       $38.3 Bln\par            Nov.   9       $38.5 Bln\par            Nov.   2       $38.5 Bln\par            Oct.  26       $38.8 Bln RECORD HIGH\par            Oct.  19       $38.6 Bln\par            Oct.  12       $38.6 Bln\par            Oct.   5       $38.4 Bln\par            Sept.  7       $37.4 Bln\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Web site:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK