\par\par \b \uc2  Rouble breaks key 30/dlr level, more pressure ahead. \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2001\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble broke through 30 to the dollar on the interbank market on Friday, seen as a key psychological level as this is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minimum desired year-end rate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased only slightly in morning trade, monitored closely by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it bases its official rate on this session, but it later broke through 30 on the interbank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the move had come after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed its offer of 29.95 rouble to the dollar, a rate at which it had supported the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Roubles for tomorrow delivery stood at 30.0375/30.0475 per dollar at 1050 GMT on the interbank market after 29.9410/29.9510 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  "The only reason for the dollar's rise is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has abandoned its offer," said Moscow Narodny Bank dealer Vasily Ushakov. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two weeks at 29.95. Dealers had estimated that the bank had spent some more than $1.0 billion over that time in supporting the rouble. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rate at the unified session, so called as it brings together eight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchanges across \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had stayed above 30 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar sales of some $70-80 million at 29.9549 roubles per dollar. \par \par \uc2  This allowed the bank to keep the rouble's average rate at the session, which serves as the base for the official next-day rate, at 29.9527 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  This was after a previous 29.9165. Trade volume at the Friday unified session was a high $150 million and the official rate was set at 29.95 roubles per dollar after 29.92. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to support the rouble on the interbank market above 30. "The way up (for the dollar) is open," Ushakov said, adding that the bank would probably maintain its presence on the unified session. \par \par \uc2  He also said banks had plenty of roubles, despite the fact that their balances at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an indicator of bank liquidity, were falling and that tax payments were due. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer was more cautious. "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not support the rouble at 29.95, the next stop will be 30.10 roubles per dollar, especially as (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Viktor) Gerashchenko has mentioned this level," he said. \par \par \uc2  He was referring to comments made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head in November, when Gerashchenko seemed to indicate that 30.10 was his floor for the rouble. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011207dxc700m89\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
