\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  rbl firms to 29.25/dlr as cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2001\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, July 25 (Reuters) - Repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the rouble to recover losses against the dollar on Wednesday and dealers expect the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average for today settlement firmed to 29.2491 per dollar on Wednesday from 29.2797 per dollar on Tuesday in a unified session of eight exchanges. Volume ticked up to $121.51 million from previous $121.42 million. \par \par \uc2  Based as usual on the session's results, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its official next-day rate to 29.25 per dollar after a previous 29.28 per dollar . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively today, starting from 29.29 roubles per dollar and gradually lowering the price to 29.25," said Alfa-Bank dealer Alexei Bukleyev. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $400 million on interbank market and some $30 million in the unified trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the aim was to support the rouble and cut the exchange rate to buy dollar revenues from exporters at a lower price to boost its reserves, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Russia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves stood at an all-time high of $35.6 billion on July 13, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Viktor Gerashchenko has said he wants reserves at $45 billion to provide for economic stability. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rouble would continue gaining in strength until the end of July, propped up by a traditional end-of-the-month need for roubles to pay taxes and by a shortage of liquidity after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  "The banks may well have overbought dollars and it may trigger a rouble deficit. So the rouble may rise to 29.20 per dollar by the end of July," said Irina Zuyeva, a dealer at Derzhava bank. \par \par \uc2  However, dollar demand was likely to increase at such low levels and the rouble would fall to 29.30 at the start of August, she said. \par \par \uc2  By 0950 GMT, roubles for tomorrow settlement were firmer, quoted at 29.2400/29.2500 in afternoon exchange trade after a previous average of 29.2899. \par \par \uc2  Roubles were traded at 29.25-29.27 on the interbank market. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010725dx7p00c3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
