\par\par \b \uc2  Russian rbl falls to 28.65/dlr, seen stabilised. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, March 2, (Reuters) - The Russian rouble lost three kopecks against the dollar in thin trade on Friday as fresh rouble liquidity hit trade, but dealers said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise near current levels next week. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average at a unified session of eight exchanges fell to 28.6514 roubles per dollar on Friday after 28.6227 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its official next day rouble rate to 28.65 per dollar , after a previous 28.62, based as usual on the results of the unified trading session. \par \par \uc2  "The situation with rouble liquidity improved after a crunch at the end of last month and the first day of this month. New roubles appeared on the market...and the rouble fell," said a Russian bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered dollars for sale at 28.68 roubles per dollar on the interbank market, indicating a possible new support level, but banks did not want to buy, considering the price too high. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $50 million in unified trade at 28.62-28.64 roubles per dollar and was apparently buying dollars directly from banks, aiming to restock reserves that have fallen after earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves fell to $28.7 billion on February 23 after $28.9 billion on February 16, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Unified trade volume was a thin $88.05 million after a previous $97.25 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rouble was likely to stabilise around the current level next week as both commercial banks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be satisfied with the current situation. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like demand and supply are balanced... They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) have managed once again to establish stability. The market does not want to buy more (dollars). Everybody is satisfied," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the rouble was likely to fall in March and hit 29.00 per dollar level within a couple of month as international prices for oil, Russia's main export, were sliding. \par \par \uc2  Rumours about a possible government reshuffle added pressure to the market and could push the rouble down, the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  By 1100 GMT, roubles for tomorrow delivery were weaker, quoted at 28.6750/28.6800 in afternoon trade after a previous average of 28.6614 roubles per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Roubles on the interbank market were quoted at 28.68-28.70 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3205l7c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
