\par\par \b \uc2  Russian rbl plummets to 28.48/dlr, cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Julie Tolkacheva \par \uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2001\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Jan 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rouble lost 32 kopecks against the dollar on Thursday in one of the sharpest falls since the 1998 devaluation as heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to offset seasonal factors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average for today settlement at the key unified trading session of eight Russian exchanges fell to 28.4750 per dollar from a previous 28.1633 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its official next day rouble rate, based as usual on the results of the morning trade, to 28.48 from 28.16 per dollar . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the plunge was due to seasonal factors as clients snapped up dollars while hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply was low. \par \par \uc2  "The week before and the week after the New Year mean a weaker inflow of dollars to Russia, because of Christmas holidays in the West," Alexander Zhukov, head of the State Duma lower house budget committee, told Ekho Moskvy radio. \par \par \uc2  He suggested the government was buying hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to repay foreign debt. "I think it is a temporary, seasonal phenomenon," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had apparently sold between $200-$300 million in unified trade and on the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  Moscow Narodny Bank dealer Vasily Ushakov said the rouble could have fallen to 28.70 per dollar or lower but for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the unified session followed the interbank market which opened at 28.60 roubles per dollar. "The (dollar) demand is colossal," he said. "Clients are ready to take dollars at whatever price. Everyone feels it." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  met some of the dollar demand that had built up since December 27, the last unified trading session before the New Year. \par \par \uc2  They said the rouble had traded on the interbank market at 28.45/28.70 per dollar between December 27 and January 3. \par \par \uc2  Ushakov said banks' strong rouble liquidity had contributed to the weakening of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Banks' balances on their correspondent accounts at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an indicator of the banking system's liquidity, fell on Thursday from Wednesday levels, but were still high at 122.63 billion roubles. \par \par \uc2  Moskomprivatbank dealer Ruslan Shcherbakov forecast the rouble would hold stable in the next few days. "Judging by how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported the rate, I think there is no reason for the rate to fall," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 1015 GMT roubles for tomorrow delivery were stronger at 28.4450/28.4600 per dollar after a previous average of 28.5678 per dollar on December 27. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1405pdn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
