\par\par \b \uc2  Pressure on rouble rises,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Julie Tolkacheva \par \uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2000\par 13:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Wednesday in an attempt to defend the rouble which has been under pressure this week but investors' appetite for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to continue, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers warned that heavy rouble supply coupled with seasonal factors could soon break \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support and push the rouble down to 28.00 per dollar from the current 27.75. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average for today settlement at a unified trading session of eight Russian exchanges, usually tightly controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was virtually flat at 27.7547 per dollar from 27.7549 per dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Based as usual on the results of the morning session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its official next day rate unchanged at 27.75 per dollar . \par \par \uc2  "The sentiment is that a bull trend (for the dollar) has started and quite a strong one," said Raiffeisen Bank treasurer Sergei Monin. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped five kopecks back yesterday and that increased the sentiment even more, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did the right thing to cool the demand at a higher rate." \par \par \uc2  Roubles for tomorrow settlement had fallen by 1030 GMT to 27.7810/27.7900 after a previous average of 27.7641. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised dealers on Tuesday after weeks of tranquillity by cutting its official next day rate to 27.75 per dollar from the previous 27.70. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR DEMAND CONTINUES \par \par \uc2  Seasonal demand for dollars from banks' clients and banks, for which the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is the only way to invest their plethora of roubles, could persuade the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to let the rouble ease more, for the sake of its dollar reserves. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily for the last three days to stop the dollar from rising. But despite such massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , high demand for dollars persists," said Alfa-Bank dealer Alexei Bukleyev. \par \par \uc2  Monin said the 28.00 per dollar level would balance the market for some time offering banks a chance to take profits. \par \par \uc2  But Bukleyev said he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the rouble to ease by about five kopecks more in the next few days. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Viktor Gerashchenko said last week he did not see the rouble moving sharply in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  Bukleyev said the rouble would be more stable on Thursday, the last day of the month, when banks and companies have to pay taxes, but could fall significantly on Friday. \par \par \uc2  He said the market could be nearing an explosion as banks rushed to buy dollars as soon as the rouble started weakening. \par \par \uc2  "If there is any movement down (in oil prices), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can spend all its reserves in two or three days, everything it has bought during the last half year." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have been slipping in the last two weeks for the first time since the start of the year reaching $23.4 billion on August 18. \par \par \uc2  "One of the questions is why should the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spend the reserves here (on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)? Can they afford to spend their reserves to sterilise the rouble - that is the question," Monin said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8u09flt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
