\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  rouble flat at 27.71/dlr as cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2000\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble was unchanged for the second day in a row, and dealers said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had again beaten off an attack on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average for today settlement at a unified trading session of eight Russian exchanges, usually tightly controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was flat at 27.7148 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Based as usual on the results of the morning session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its official rate unchanged at 27.71 per dollar . \par \par \uc2  "There has been a strong demand for dollars for several days in a row due to seasonal factors, because the dollar usually rises at the start of autumn," said Alfa-Bank dealer Alexei Bukleyev. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is trying to accumulate long positions ahead of the end of summer." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had apparently sold about $100 million to support the rouble. \par \par \uc2  Bukleyev said banks channelled most free funds to the market. \par \par \uc2  Despite the fact the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily over the last several days, commercial banks' balances at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which indicate banks' liquidity, have been rising. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stubbornly unwilling to let it (the dollar) rise," Bukleyev said. \par \par \uc2  "If it (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) keeps holding the rate as it has been, it will knock off the demand which will lead to a fall (of the dollar.)" \par \par \uc2  He forecast the fall could be by two to three kopecks. \par \par \uc2  "If it (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) abandons (the market) one day...the dollar will start rising sharply, by about 10 kopecks a day before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to fix it a certain level," Bukleyev said. \par \par \uc2  In afternoon trade, roubles for tomorrow settlement were slightly stronger, quoted at 27.7310/27.7370 at 0850 GMT after a previous average of 27.7439 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8n0aqgm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
