\par\par \b \uc2  Russia c.bank says rouble support changed mkt mood. \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 1999\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Nov 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble against the dollar on Monday and has succeeded in changing the mood of the market, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We carried out \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in volumes sufficient to change the mood of market participants," said the official, who declined to be named. "Those banks which buy dollars today in the Unified Trading System will be disappointed," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Unified Trading Session involves eight exchanges throughout Russia and its average rate serves as the basis for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official rate, which tumbled 10 kopecks to a new low of 26.49 per dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is under our control," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. He gave no details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a net buyer of dollars in November. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rouble would have fallen further on Monday were it not for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. One said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 26.50 per dollar and would probably try to maintain that level through the next few days. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Viktor Gerashchenko has said the rouble will finish the year at 27 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Artyom Danielyan, Moscow Newsroom, +7 095 941 8520, moscow.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbn09g16\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
