\par\par \b \uc2  Russian c.bank spent reserves on debt, not rouble. \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 18:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 3 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $500 million in the third week of July to service foreign debt, not to defend the rouble, Russia's special envoy to international financial organisations said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  simply repaid $500 million out of a $1 billion loan (to the International Monetary Fund)," envoy Mikhail Zadornov told radio Ekho Moskvy. "There has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market", he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves fell by $500 million on July 23 to $11.0 billion. They were down $1.1 billion for the month and at their lowest level since April. \par \par \uc2  Zadornov said the bank recently has not been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which has generally seen the rouble appreciate or hold steady against the dollar, and he called a downturn on Tuesday "a normal correction". \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rouble rate eased on Tuesday to 24.22 per dollar from a previous 24.19. \par \par \uc2  Zadornov forecast the rouble would gradually fall in line with inflation but would not reach 32 per dollar before the second half of 2000. \par \par \uc2  Zadornov said an IMF mission was expected in Moscow on August 24 to review conditions ahead of disbursement of a second tranche of the $4.5 billion loan the Fund agreed last week. \par \par \uc2  The first $640 million tranche was disbursed at the end of last week, and the second tranche is expected in September. \par \par \uc2  ((Svetlana Kovalyova, Moscow Newsroom +7 095 941 8520, moscow.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv83037sb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
