\par\par \b \uc2  Russia rouble up at 24.21/dlr, IMF loan seen helping. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Karl Emerick Hanuska \par \uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 14:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, July 29 (Reuters) - The rouble firmed against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, averaging 24.2104 per dollar versus a previous 24.2214, a day after the International Monetary Fund resumed lending to Russia. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's board of directors on Wednesday voted to release a first tranche of $640 million from an 18-month $4.5 billion loan, a move one prominent parliamentarian said would ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The credit will enable the government to make payments on its foreign debt without money from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Alexander Zhukov, head of the budget committee in the State Duma lower house, told Itar-Tass news agency. \par \par \uc2  "That will give Russia the opportunity to build up its foreign reserves, which is one of the most important tasks toward strengthening the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Thursday that by July 23 its reserves had fallen to a three-month low of $11.0 billion, down $500 million from a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Economists attributed the reduction to heavy foreign debt obligations and rouble underpinning. Some estimated the bank spent up to $300 million on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Mikhail Zadornov, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's special envoy to international financial organisations, was quoted by Itar-Tass as saying the government had plans to allow the rouble to fluctuate relative to the rate of inflation. \par \par \uc2  In Washington, Zadornov spoke to journalists after the IMF loan was announced but would not say when the rouble plans would be put into action or give any further details. \par \par \uc2  Over the last month the official rouble rate, which is based on the results of unified trade on the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange's electronic SELT system, has dropped about one percent against the dollar under \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. \par \par \uc2  But inflation in the first three weeks alone of July was 2.2 percent month-on-month. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official exchange rate\tab   for Friday firmer at 24.21 per dollar, after 24.22, three days in a row.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 1120 GMT roubles for tomorrow settlement on SELT were quoted at 24.2301/24.2520 per dollar after a previous average of 24.2543.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Spot roubles, for day-after-next settlement, were at 24.2000/24.5000     per dollar. No spot deals were reached on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941-8520 moscow.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7t03fs0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
