\par\par \b \uc2  Russian c.bank says rouble holds without support. \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 18:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, March 15 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that rules on repatriating foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were keeping the rouble stable and that for the first time in years it had not had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. \par \par \uc2  The rouble crashed after August 1998, when the government was forced to let it float. It later ceased market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but introduced rules to bring hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by making exporters repatriate 75 percent of their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market all the previous years in January," Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Viktor Melnikov told a round-table talk of businessmen and politicians at parliament's Federation Council upper house. \par \par \uc2  "In January 1998, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to throw $3.4 billion on the market to support the rouble. This year, for the first time in all these years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January as exporters' revenues held us." \par \par \uc2  He said the daily flow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country rose 40 percent between October 1998 and February 1999 and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected the volume to rise a further five percent in March. However, he gave no figures or comparisons. \par \par \uc2  Despite the government order to exporters, mainly oil and gas and metals producers, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves keep shrinking as it helps the finance ministry make debt repayments. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also say Russia suffers from endemic capital flight but Melnikov said only 5.2 percent of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due for sale in Russia did not return under the repatriation order. \par \par \uc2  He called for a law which would require a special permit for export \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the current system allowed short-lived companies to launder money and export it. \par \par \uc2  Capital flight often takes place via fake import contracts, when the importer presents a contract to the government for permission to send cash abroad to pay for goods which never actually arrive in Russia. \par \par \uc2  ((Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow newsroom, +075 941-8520 moscow.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv3f02zh6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
