\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ruble Up As Bks Meet Dlr Needs, Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1999\par 16:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble (RUB) inched up in average volumes Thursday as commercial banks had temporarily met their need for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support for the ruble at RUB23.00 against the dollar helped the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange's open trading session the ruble for next-day delivery eased to RUB22.90 from RUB23.07 Wednesday. Volume totaled $150 million. \par \par \uc2  However, spot ruble fell slightly to RUB22.77 against the dollar at the trading session reserved for exporters and importers. Wednesday, that session closed at RUB22.70 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the official dollar rate at RUB22.77 to the dollar, up from RUB22.67 Wednesday. Volume rose to $80 million, up from $50 million Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and gold) reserves dropped by\par $300 million last week," a trader with a major Western bank in Moscow\par noted, referring to the fact that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the market, selling dollars to participants.\par    "Banks have been buying sufficiently for now," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday, its gross reserves dropped to $11.6\par billion last Friday from $11.9 billion a week earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1518GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1150 1855 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1s00rjs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
