\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Wall Street Journal - Aug 27. \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, August 27 (Reuters) - The Wall Street Journal reported the following business stories in its electronic edition Thursday: \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to plunge. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also cancelled dollar trading on the Moscow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange. Credit Suisse and its First Boston unit said profits were hit by Russia's economic woes. Moscow's moves roiled world markets, and U.S. stocks fell 79.30 points to 8523.35. \par \par \uc2  * Some on Wall Street believe the Fed could be forced to cut interest rates in the coming months to address the global crisis, though the prospects of an imminent rate cut seem slim. \par \par \uc2  * Northwest Airlines  cancelled hundreds of weekend flights because of a threatened walkout by pilots if agreement on a new labour contract isn't reached by midnight tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  * A former lawyer for Liggett  plans to testify the company believed rivals would retaliate if it continued work on a safer cigarette. Meanwhile, R.J. Reynolds  and Brown & Williamson  said they are dropping out of settlement talks with a group of states. \par \par \uc2  * Durable-goods orders shot up 2.4 percent last month, marking the biggest rise in eight months, mainly driven by businesses investing in new technology. \par \par \uc2  * An FTC judge ordered the Trans Union credit-reporting agency to stop selling marketing lists with consumer credit data, citing privacy protection. \par \par \uc2  * Quark's CEO said his company's move on Adobe  was earnest, though he offered few details on how Quark would fund the offer for the much larger firm. Adobe shares rose 13 percent. \par \par \uc2  * Microsoft  engineers discussed the idea of a software bug for Windows that would halt a competitor's operating-system software in 1991, according to documents in two lawsuits brought by the government and a tiny rival. \par \par \uc2  * Intel  said it supplied documents and other evidence about its relationship with Microsoft for use in the Justice Department's investigation. \par \par \uc2  * Priceline.com named former Citicorp  President Richard Braddock as CEO of the Internet commerce firm. \par \par \uc2  * U.S. airports are attacking proposed EU rules on the pending alliance of British Airways  and American , which could force the partners to cut flights between the U.S. and Europe. \par \par \uc2  * The SEC suffered a blow to its insider-trading enforcement as a U.S. appeals court ruled the government must show a corporate insider actually used inside information to trade. \par \par \uc2  * Anheuser-Busch  plans to raise beer prices for the first time in nearly two years, in a move expected to boost the price of a case of beer by 2 percent to 4 percent. \par \par \uc2  * Merck  agreed to settle with the FTC to end an antitrust probe into its ownership of the former Medco. \par \par \uc2  * Japanese bond yields fell to 1.105 percent - a record low for Japan and possibly the lowest ever - amid investors' concerns about the economy. \par \par \uc2  * Canadian farmers will harvest their smallest spring wheat crop in 10 years, a government agency forecast. \par \par \uc2  ((New York News Desk 212 859-1700)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8r01qh2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
